    {
      "ts": "2026-02-13T00:22:32.885-08:00",
      "player": "DSV3 Analyst",
      "type": "llm_response",
      "reasoning": "Ah! I see: \"DSV3 Analyst loses 1 life at combat from Multiversal Passage\" and \"loses 2 life at combat from Formidable Speaker\". So I took 3 damage total. My Eddymurk Crab didn't prevent the damage! Why?\n\
\n\
Oh! Eddymurk Crab says \"When {this} enters, tap up to two target creatures.\" The tapping happens when it enters, but if the creatures are already attacking, tapping them doesn't remove them from combat! In Magic, tapping an attacking creature doesn't remove it from combat or prevent its damage. Once a creature is declared as an attacker, tapping it doesn't matter - it still deals combat damage.\n\
\n\
So my play was bad! I wasted Eddymurk Crab for no benefit. I should have cast it BEFORE attackers were declared, or cast it on my turn. Now I have a tapped 5/5 and I still took damage.\n\
\n\
Lesson learned: tapping attackers after they're declared doesn't prevent damage.\n\
\n\
Now it's my turn (T4), I'm at 9 life. I have a tapped Eddymurk Crab (5/5). I have 5 lands (1 tapped from casting Eddymurk Crab? Actually 4 tapped? Let me check battlefield).\n\
